Small and medium businesses need Mashbot to manage their presence across multiple social networks through a consistent service. Staff should be able to connect external accounts, prepare campaigns, schedule content for simultaneous publication, manage contributor, approver, and publisher roles, respond to audience activity, and monitor keywords and campaign history. The service should reduce the effort required to coordinate marketing and customer engagement across changing platforms.

Current Slots:
[
  {
    "name": "project_goals",
    "category": "goals",
    "value": "Help small and medium businesses manage social media more efficiently with less manual coordination across platforms, maintain a consistent presence, respond faster to audience activity, and reduce effort in planning and publishing campaigns."
  },
  {
    "name": "stakeholder_roles",
    "category": "stakeholders",
    "value": "Staff users who connect external social accounts, create and schedule campaigns, and manage contributor, approver, and publisher roles."
  },
  {
    "name": "functional_needs",
    "category": "functionality",
    "value": "Connect external social accounts; create and schedule campaigns for multiple networks simultaneously; manage contributor, approver, and publisher roles; respond to comments and messages; monitor keywords; maintain campaign history."
  },
  {
    "name": "business_rules",
    "category": "business_logic",
    "value": "Contributors can draft and submit content, but cannot publish directly unless they also have publisher rights. Approvers must review content before it goes live. Most campaigns use a single approval step, but sensitive campaigns may require a second approval. If content is edited after approval, it must return to review."
  },
  {
    "name": "data_entities",
    "category": "data",
    "value": "External social accounts, campaigns, roles (contributor, approver, publisher), audience interactions such as comments and messages, monitored keywords, and campaign history."
  },
  {
    "name": "constraints",
    "category": "constraints",
    "value": null
  },
  {
    "name": "quality_concerns",
    "category": "quality",
    "value": "Efficient management, reduced manual coordination, consistent cross-platform presence, faster response to audience activity, and clear traceability of campaign history."
  },
  {
    "name": "boundary_conditions",
    "category": "exceptions",
    "value": null
  },
  {
    "name": "business_rules_content_approval_policy",
    "category": "business_logic",
    "value": "Contributors may submit drafts but cannot publish unless they also have publisher rights; approvers review content before publication; a single approval is typical, with optional second approval for sensitive campaigns; edited content after approval must be sent back to review."
  },
  {
    "name": "business_rules_campaign_history_retention",
    "category": "business_logic",
    "value": null
  },
  {
    "name": "constraints_social_platform_api_access",
    "category": "constraints",
    "value": null
  },
  {
    "name": "boundary_conditions_account_connection_failure_handling",
    "category": "exceptions",
    "value": null
  },
  {
    "name": "quality_concerns_auditability_and_traceability",
    "category": "quality",
    "value": "Maintain a clear history of campaigns so teams can track what was done and learn from it."
  },
  {
    "name": "approval_escalation_triggers",
    "category": "business_logic",
    "value": "Additional approval or review is required for high-risk or brand-sensitive content such as regulated promotions, pricing changes, legal statements, crisis-related posts, posts mentioning major partners or public issues, very large audience posts, posts with paid promotion, or content using non-standard material such as user-generated content or controversial topics; exact thresholds must be configurable by the business."
  },
  {
    "name": "multi_step_approval_workflow",
    "category": "functionality",
    "value": "The workflow normally uses a single approval step, but may require a second approval for sensitive, high-risk, or brand-sensitive campaigns based on configurable business rules."
  },
  {
    "name": "post_approval_edit_revalidation_rules",
    "category": "business_logic",
    "value": "If content is edited after approval, it must go back into review because the approved version has changed."
  },
  {
    "name": "approval_audit_trail",
